    {
      "id": "broken-oaths",
      "title": "Broken Oaths",
      "playstyle": "Scout-led feints and Raider breaches drive opposing formations out of position, then remove attachments and convert Exhaustion into Command pressure.",
      "hypothesis": "Can a Scout/Skirmisher/Raider setup create meaningful Strength denial and attached-layer theft, or does plain Force Strength still win?",
      "combo_notes": [
        "Seven Black Ships, River Raiders and Seized the Standard Of can remove attached layers after the opposing Frontline opens; The Muster Was False offers another Bond-punishment line with a Scout or Seer.",
        "Wolf Skirmishers, Ilyri, Salt-Road Fleet and The Line Was Baited threaten meaningful Rearward movement, Depleted and Shaken, while Had Been Ordered Forward enables opportunistic Maneuvers.",
        "Lantern Scouts and Lysa support They Were Gathering There, The Scouts Had Warned Them and Before Sunset for actual Strength or Guarded counterplay, not merely looking at cards.",
        "Shaken Raider/Skirmisher pressure makes Shared the Spoils With and The Trap Closed useful; The Line Had Begun to Move can tax one crowded Front while Bought Time For refills."
      ],
      "combo_packages": [
        {
          "label": "Breach then steal attachments",
          "enablers": [
            "seven-black-ships",
            "the-river-raiders",
            "the-aradai",
            "rovan-the-gatebreaker"
          ],
